434
00:42:57,626 --> 00:42:59,510
So it is all down to you.

435
00:42:59,550 --> 00:43:08,244
David Budaya kicks us off having a much, much better series of dives so far.

436
00:43:08,925 --> 00:43:13,333
This forward four and a half somersault tucked is worth 3.7.

437
00:43:17,802 --> 00:43:21,766
Very tidy as his top scoring dive in the prelims with an 88.8.

438
00:43:21,867 --> 00:43:27,333
It's a bit of a rush to reach the vertical with this dive because there's so many somersaults to get through.

439
00:43:27,773 --> 00:43:30,237
Just powers off the end of the platform.

440
00:43:34,021 --> 00:43:36,023
In fact, he almost over rotated it, didn't he?

441
00:43:36,063 --> 00:43:41,751
But to control the entry once more, he's having a much better session here second time around.

442
00:43:42,202 --> 00:43:51,731
Remember, this is the guy who does confess that he has a bit of a fear of heights, which is a strange complaint when you want to be a 10-meter platform diver.

443
00:43:52,112 --> 00:43:53,853
That's a new high mark for him into the 90s.

444
00:43:53,893 --> 00:43:56,456
He didn't manage that last night.

445
00:43:57,976 --> 00:43:59,637
So he's come to compete.

446
00:43:59,657 --> 00:44:00,900
Jose Guerra from Cuba.

447
00:44:05,023 --> 00:44:08,286
Down in tenth position, in with three and a half somersault, three point two.

448
00:44:09,527 --> 00:44:11,568
So he can't afford to get too much wrong here.

449
00:44:13,945 --> 00:44:14,887
We got it all right.

450
00:44:14,947 --> 00:44:26,385
And again, that's close, isn't it?

451
00:44:29,570 --> 00:44:35,500
You take out his disastrous second dive in the prelims with a 21.6 that we've referred to a couple of times.

452
00:44:35,760 --> 00:44:38,204
How much further up the rankings would he have been?

453
00:44:39,746 --> 00:44:41,268
Give him another 50 points.

454
00:44:43,965 --> 00:44:45,628
He's got the good dives coming.

455
00:44:47,690 --> 00:44:50,875
Gleb Gauperin, the 27-year-old from Moscow.

456
00:44:52,036 --> 00:44:54,039
Double world champion, double Olympic bronze.

457
00:44:55,161 --> 00:44:57,063
He's the man, remember, who's had all the injury worries.

458
00:44:59,106 --> 00:45:01,128
Forward three and a half, somersault there.

459
00:45:01,628 --> 00:45:05,434
Just a 3.0 degree of difficulty.

460
00:45:07,945 --> 00:45:10,510
So Galperin had some problems with his second dive.

461
00:45:11,572 --> 00:45:12,594
Low tariff here.

462
00:45:12,996 --> 00:45:16,402
He's going to have to fight back with his last three.

463
00:45:20,692 --> 00:45:22,976
Good scores, but only a three tariff.

464
00:45:25,242 --> 00:45:25,583
So 72.

465
00:45:29,393 --> 00:45:35,420
You'll know what's coming next with Peter Waterfield having a really disappointing evening last night.

466
00:45:35,501 --> 00:45:39,927
Tom Daley is carrying British hopes entirely on his young shoulders.

467
00:45:40,547 --> 00:45:43,771
Arm stand back, triple somersault, 3.5.

468
00:45:46,695 --> 00:45:49,940
No towel for extra grip for Tom.

469
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:54,186
See how long he holds the dive right at the top.

470
00:45:56,748 --> 00:46:00,853
This was Tom's top scoring dive in prelims with an 89.

471
00:46:08,983 --> 00:46:10,525
Very impressive on the platform.

472
00:46:10,565 --> 00:46:11,586
Looks so in control.

473
00:46:12,788 --> 00:46:13,389
Good push.

474
00:46:14,851 --> 00:46:18,494
Just not quite 100% vertical with the entry.

475
00:46:19,536 --> 00:46:21,438
But the judges are going to like most of this.

476
00:46:24,742 --> 00:46:30,389
crowd trying to put a little bit of pressure on the judges to maybe convince them that it was slightly better than it was.

477
00:46:32,251 --> 00:46:39,438
So he's not 100% vertical and he's not 100% square either, but it's a very good dive in every other aspect.

478
00:46:43,501 --> 00:46:47,306
Great line, toes pointed from fingers to toes.

479
00:46:47,987 --> 00:46:52,692
And an 84 there, just five points short of last night's effort.

480
00:46:54,561 --> 00:46:56,465
Victor from Russia.

481
00:46:56,505 --> 00:46:59,708
Reverse three and a half somersault tucked.

482
00:47:02,112 --> 00:47:04,195
Experiencing in a big games for the first time.

483
00:47:10,403 --> 00:47:11,905
Very composed and waiting.

484
00:47:13,027 --> 00:47:19,235
He's got his mind completely right and clear.

485
00:47:23,079 --> 00:47:30,231
jumped well away from the platform, but that didn't compromise the somersaults or his entry position.

486
00:47:32,235 --> 00:47:42,612
This dive too, from that standing position close to the platform, you can have a worry, but he took that out of the equation in a bar by taking himself well away.

487
00:47:43,853 --> 00:47:45,155
Lots of clearance room there.

488
00:47:49,625 --> 00:47:52,007
to compromise those if you jump out rather than up.

489
00:47:53,367 --> 00:47:55,010
You can find yourself short of time but not that.

490
00:47:55,590 --> 00:48:00,554
Seventy-nine point two is very solid.

491
00:48:00,574 --> 00:48:08,380
Columbia's Victor Ortega who was taken diving when he was just three years of age.

492
00:48:09,961 --> 00:48:11,724
He's back in seventeenth position.

493
00:48:11,943 --> 00:48:19,210
So, this arm stand back triple somersault

494
00:48:23,273 --> 00:48:24,434
Oh well it didn't really.

495
00:48:29,744 --> 00:48:32,288
Larger splash, didn't control the entry.

496
00:48:37,675 --> 00:48:40,740
So just modest scores coming in in the sevens.

497
00:48:40,762 --> 00:48:45,989
3.3 the difficulty.

498
00:48:48,045 --> 00:48:49,668
We discussed that tattoo.

499
00:48:49,688 --> 00:48:52,490
It's about his love of life.

500
00:48:54,052 --> 00:48:55,293
Life in Spanish is a Vita.

501
00:48:57,556 --> 00:48:58,097
But it's life.

502
00:48:58,438 --> 00:49:00,039
69-3, that's life.

503
00:49:00,179 --> 00:49:01,380
Don't always get the scores you want.

504
00:49:03,364 --> 00:49:04,824
Whoever said life is supposed to be fair.

505
00:49:06,827 --> 00:49:08,108
Anton Sakharov next.

506
00:49:09,490 --> 00:49:13,394
He's just above the cut at 11th, this forward four and a half somersault.

507
00:49:15,231 --> 00:49:15,813
Oh, nice.

508
00:49:16,393 --> 00:49:16,954
Very good.

509
00:49:18,534 --> 00:49:19,956
Of this four and a half somersault.

510
00:49:21,117 --> 00:49:22,199
The divers have attempted it.

511
00:49:22,219 --> 00:49:24,460
This is one of the better efforts.

512
00:49:27,563 --> 00:49:29,085
Very tight tuck position.

513
00:49:30,726 --> 00:49:33,650
And eights across the board for Zakharov.

514
00:49:37,434 --> 00:49:38,715
Not much to complain about there.

515
00:49:38,894 --> 00:49:39,815
Not much to deduct.

516
00:49:40,697 --> 00:49:41,177
So they don't.

517
00:49:41,358 --> 00:49:43,719
Eighty eight point eight.

518
00:49:44,492 --> 00:49:47,217
The Chinese would think that was a lucky dive with all those eights.

519
00:49:48,380 --> 00:49:49,221
That's the lucky number.

520
00:49:49,240 --> 00:49:53,168
I think they prefer a hundred and eight.

521
00:49:54,789 --> 00:49:55,490
Don't rule it out.

522
00:49:55,751 --> 00:49:57,635
Riley McCormick from Canada.

523
00:49:59,778 --> 00:50:03,083
Trains and studies at Arizona State University in the States.

524
00:50:03,204 --> 00:50:10,737
This is an inward three and a half somersault and he's just out of the picture in 14th at the moment.

525
00:50:19,880 --> 00:50:25,568
Eric Sane went out to the competition last night.

526
00:50:25,628 --> 00:50:31,335
Canada would be disappointed if they didn't have a finalist in this 10 metre competition.

527
00:50:34,260 --> 00:50:39,347
McCoury's going to have to find something in the second half of this semi-final.

528
00:50:39,467 --> 00:50:45,617
That was close to just the feet rolled over a little.

529
00:50:46,829 --> 00:50:50,114
just to leave less than the 100% impression for the judges.

530
00:50:54,219 --> 00:50:54,900
Eighty-one six.

531
00:50:57,585 --> 00:50:59,907
Going to be tight around that cutoff point.

532
00:51:02,932 --> 00:51:04,193
from Cuba.

533
00:51:07,820 --> 00:51:09,461
Back three and a half somersault.

534
00:51:11,838 --> 00:51:14,521
a couple of Olympic Games, two World Championships.

535
00:51:15,264 --> 00:51:21,434
He would regard a final position as reward for the training and the dedication.

536
00:51:27,943 --> 00:51:28,304
Oh dear.

537
00:51:28,686 --> 00:51:30,367
Well, he had trouble with his dive last night.

538
00:51:30,429 --> 00:51:38,621
Sixty-four point eight only and the judges aren't going to be too

539
00:51:40,356 --> 00:51:41,657
His issues with the entry.

540
00:51:44,260 --> 00:51:45,282
He was well short.

541
00:51:47,003 --> 00:51:49,527
Almost disastrously so in terms of the scores.

542
00:51:51,469 --> 00:51:56,813
Fives and a five and a half for fifty five point eight and that will be tough to recover from.

543
00:51:56,873 --> 00:52:05,182
The defending champion, Matthew Mitcham.

544
00:52:06,175 --> 00:52:09,340
Only non-Chinese diver to winner medal in Beijing.

545
00:52:10,521 --> 00:52:11,684
Ruined for clean sweep.

546
00:52:12,005 --> 00:52:13,567
In with three and a half somersault now.

547
00:52:23,684 --> 00:52:24,364
Oh, beautiful.

548
00:52:24,625 --> 00:52:26,427
He's back to near his best.

549
00:52:32,197 --> 00:52:48,416
3.2 yes he does like it he loves a smile for the camera doesn't he he loves this stage well he is a showman and to be fair even during the difficulties last night he came up smiling and waving at the camera

550
00:52:49,038 --> 00:52:52,983
I think he's one of those athletes, Roger, who just finds it a joy to be here.

551
00:52:53,603 --> 00:52:54,824
Wow, I'm at the Olympics.

552
00:52:55,126 --> 00:52:58,630
He's done it all before, but he just thrives on it.

553
00:52:58,650 --> 00:53:00,572
And an 86.4 for Matthew.

554
00:53:00,632 --> 00:53:06,400
So he's picked up another five points on his prelim effort for the same dive.

555
00:53:06,880 --> 00:53:14,168
If he's feeling enjoyment and no pressure, that makes him even more dangerous if he can relax into his diving.

556
00:53:15,431 --> 00:53:18,775
Nick McCrory now from the United States, 13th.

557
00:53:20,155 --> 00:53:26,362
That was a forward four and a half somersault with a three point seven tariff, which he will have been looking to cash in on.

558
00:53:26,884 --> 00:53:36,195
He just sounded a little heavy footed on the platform and I'm not quite sure he really had a vertical body on the entry here.

559
00:53:36,255 --> 00:53:42,163
The replay will show us not that the judges see this, but he was just still working his way out.

560
00:53:43,476 --> 00:53:46,722
of the somersaults as he entered the water and so still bent at the hips.

561
00:53:47,643 --> 00:53:50,608
So just held him back a little on his marks because of that.

562
00:53:54,393 --> 00:53:55,615
83.25.

563
00:53:56,797 --> 00:53:57,398
High tariff.

564
00:53:58,420 --> 00:53:58,960
So that helps.

565
00:54:03,547 --> 00:54:06,632
Alexander Bondar from Ukraine.

566
00:54:07,514 --> 00:54:11,019
Fifteenth arm stand back, double somersault, two and a half twist.

567
00:54:11,336 --> 00:54:14,922
This was his problem last night, 57.6 for this dive.

568
00:54:15,603 --> 00:54:16,945
So keep your fingers crossed for him.

569
00:54:27,541 --> 00:54:35,353
Long hold.

570
00:54:40,362 --> 00:54:43,786
Well, it's better than last night, but there's still room there.

571
00:54:45,128 --> 00:54:47,753
It's a real worry when they stay up there that long.

572
00:54:50,016 --> 00:55:00,190
The ankles were never together until entry, really, and it wasn't quite vertical, but he's got away with one in terms of improvement from last night.

573
00:55:02,273 --> 00:55:03,635
Leg form was pretty ropey.

574
00:55:06,146 --> 00:55:11,012
One of the great things about the Games is how you sense that the crowd are supporting every competitor.

575
00:55:11,072 --> 00:55:17,280
Obviously the Brits are getting a massive support, but you do feel in those long pauses the crowd are willing them to do it well.

576
00:55:19,083 --> 00:55:20,885
He's picked up 25 points there, Bondoy.

577
00:55:22,768 --> 00:55:25,692
High tariff on that dive, even though there were a couple of faults.

578
00:55:28,625 --> 00:55:33,269
Ivan Garcia is carrying on from where he left off last night.

579
00:55:34,572 --> 00:55:38,376
At least inward four and a half somersault four point one.

580
00:55:38,416 --> 00:55:43,581
This is a big dive and he's in third place after his opening two dives.

581
00:55:44,782 --> 00:55:46,724
Four and a half somersaults from a standing start.

582
00:55:46,885 --> 00:55:58,057
You've got to be quick.

583
00:55:58,358 --> 00:56:10,356
He was pretty quick.

584
00:56:10,878 --> 00:56:14,643
I was just looking to see how much knee bend there was going to be as he launched off the platform.

585
00:56:15,244 --> 00:56:16,646
Not a great deal really.

586
00:56:16,786 --> 00:56:19,692
He still generated good power.

587
00:56:22,456 --> 00:56:25,440
And the feet just came apart for that finish.

588
00:56:25,460 --> 00:56:29,365
That's such a shame to get from the split tuck to get the ankles together.

589
00:56:29,405 --> 00:56:31,148
Timing.

590
00:56:32,829 --> 00:56:33,331
Not easy.

591
00:56:35,112 --> 00:56:36,094
And an 86.1.

592
00:56:38,177 --> 00:56:39,239
Long hold at the top.

593
00:56:39,259 --> 00:56:47,130
You can feel the 15,000 odd people just all holding their breath, wondering when he's going to make that decision to launch.

594
00:56:47,498 --> 00:56:52,724
We were a little bit critical of that dive, but he still picked up nine points on the same one from last night.

595
00:56:54,788 --> 00:56:56,070
When I say we, it was me, wasn't it?

596
00:56:57,251 --> 00:56:57,612
Thank you.

597
00:56:58,233 --> 00:57:01,137
German Sanchez from Mexico.

598
00:57:02,900 --> 00:57:07,746
Second after the opening couple of dives.

599
00:57:08,067 --> 00:57:13,994
Arm stand back, triple somersault, and again the pool hushed.

600
00:57:17,097 --> 00:57:17,697
Oh dear.

601
00:57:20,061 --> 00:57:23,987
Entry-wise, that's a disaster at this level, and he will be punished.

602
00:57:24,206 --> 00:57:31,338
The judges do not like to see that, even if you do a lot right before then, which he seemed to do, but the timing was wrong.

603
00:57:32,219 --> 00:57:39,750
Came out too early, over-rotated, massive splash, and he's under five right across.

604
00:57:40,690 --> 00:57:42,514
Three and a half, four,

605
00:57:46,038 --> 00:57:53,568
Well, he'll get away with that in the semifinal stage, having had such an impressive start, but that's got to go if he's there tonight.

606
00:57:56,853 --> 00:58:00,559
Martin Wolfram has been outstanding.

607
00:58:01,079 --> 00:58:02,541
Reverse three and a half somersault.

608
00:58:03,983 --> 00:58:05,166
Top of the pile at the moment.

609
00:58:10,873 --> 00:58:11,735
He may stay there.

610
00:58:11,936 --> 00:58:12,737
That was a good effort.

611
00:58:15,367 --> 00:58:18,050
The degree of difficulty will just hold him back a little, a 3.3.

612
00:58:18,411 --> 00:58:31,608
He competed here in February, that World Cup event, which gave many of the divers a chance to sample the atmosphere and the water.

613
00:58:31,829 --> 00:58:40,260
He was ninth in the 10-meter platform then, but he is a bit of an unknown quantity and maybe one or two of the others will be wondering just how much this guy's got in his locker.

614
00:58:44,476 --> 00:58:47,139
79.2 for Martin.

615
00:58:50,505 --> 00:58:51,786
His lowest dive so far.

616
00:58:52,987 --> 00:59:00,759
Sasha Klein up next who slipped back a bit after good work last night and the start of today.

617
00:59:00,818 --> 00:59:05,947
Now he's got an arm stand back, triple somersault with 3.5 the tariff.

618
00:59:06,487 --> 00:59:08,289
He's in eighth place.

619
00:59:13,365 --> 00:59:16,630
Well this was his top dive in the prelims and maybe it will be again.

620
00:59:16,650 --> 00:59:20,916
92.75 last night for Sasha.

621
00:59:27,864 --> 00:59:29,385
Takes a lovely pike position.

622
00:59:33,110 --> 00:59:35,193
He did get a couple of nines for it last night.

623
00:59:36,014 --> 00:59:37,295
Eight and a halfs and eights.

624
00:59:37,976 --> 00:59:39,559
So not quite as good.

625
00:59:43,099 --> 00:59:44,121
Delightful to watch.

626
00:59:44,782 --> 00:59:45,503
Well executed.

627
00:59:46,503 --> 00:59:48,306
And an 89 to 5.

628
00:59:48,346 --> 00:59:53,811
Seems fairly happy with the way the competition is going.

629
00:59:54,452 --> 01:00:02,041
I wonder if the same can be said for Lin Yue, who will have only the very highest level of expectations.

630
01:00:02,380 --> 01:00:08,307
He's fourth after two rounds, back three and a half somersault.

631
01:00:08,327 --> 01:00:09,188
Oh, he's nailed it again.

632
01:00:09,869 --> 01:00:12,431
That was the only 100 point dive last night.

633
01:00:13,795 --> 01:00:16,018
Even Chou Bow couldn't eclipse this one.

634
01:00:20,989 --> 01:00:22,612
Oh, he's just perfect through the air.

635
01:00:29,706 --> 01:00:31,989
Unbelievable, the nine and a half's come in.

636
01:00:35,226 --> 01:00:37,289
And we're heading for three digits here.

637
01:00:38,269 --> 01:00:40,391
He got a ten there that's going to be taken out.

638
01:00:41,393 --> 01:00:45,137
But three nine and a halfs and a one hundred and two point six.

639
01:00:45,157 --> 01:00:45,677
There it is.

640
01:00:46,297 --> 01:00:48,840
Our first hundred point dive in the semi.

641
01:00:50,282 --> 01:01:04,896
There may well be a competition within the competition between these two Chinese teammates and rivals, of course, Chubo now reverse three and a half somersault and a disappointing second dive, which is really quite out of character.

642
01:01:07,559 --> 01:01:08,099
He's back.

643
01:01:09,541 --> 01:01:14,086
That's not a 100-point dive because he doesn't have the tariff, but the form is there.

644
01:01:18,213 --> 01:01:22,016
See how much deeper into a squat he gets to drive up off the platform.

645
01:01:27,864 --> 01:01:30,427
He has got a history of landing plenty of 10s.

646
01:01:32,432 --> 01:01:41,628
25 perfect tens in a series back in 2011, a FINA Diving World Series event in Beijing.

647
01:01:41,648 --> 01:01:49,681
94.05, exactly the same mark as that dive yielded last night.

648
01:01:50,876 --> 01:01:52,039
Now, this will be interesting.

649
01:01:52,539 --> 01:01:55,182
Lin Yue has taken over at the top of the leaderboard.

650
01:01:55,623 --> 01:01:58,005
David Buday has come from eighteenth to third.

651
01:01:59,969 --> 01:02:03,353
The Mexican and the Germans still holding their own.

652
01:02:03,494 --> 01:02:06,077
Tom Daly has worked his way up the field as well.

653
01:02:07,097 --> 01:02:09,621
Matthew Mitchum just ahead of the cut.

654
01:02:10,382 --> 01:02:18,353
Nick McCrory, Riley McCormack are the ones under pressure.

655
01:02:18,333 --> 01:02:22,259
12 remember the cutoff to go through to tonight's final.

656
01:02:24,181 --> 01:02:29,929
The standard has gone up a notch or two from last night.

657
01:02:31,432 --> 01:02:41,407
Well undeniably Roger, you see this across competitions, qualifying the top boys just want to get there and they're holding something back and not now.

658
01:02:43,510 --> 01:02:46,315
David Bodeo has transformed overnight.

659
01:02:53,534 --> 01:02:56,297
He's now in third place.

660
01:02:56,318 --> 01:03:01,425
Reverse three and a half somersault for his fourth dive.

661
01:03:01,445 --> 01:03:03,389
3.3 the tariff.

662
01:03:05,952 --> 01:03:07,976
Well he'll be relieved to have done a good job with that.

663
01:03:08,597 --> 01:03:11,902
That was the dive that got him only 44 points last night.

664
01:03:12,543 --> 01:03:14,746
Eliminate that from his total.

665
01:03:15,706 --> 01:03:21,516
Come up with something better which he's certainly done here and he'll continue to be knocking around the top five.

666
01:03:29,679 --> 01:03:36,088
Matthew Mitchum made mention of this man when he was talking about the inconsistent performances across the preliminaries.

667
01:03:36,108 --> 01:03:39,554
And David Baddai, he doesn't belong in 18th position and he won't be there.

668
01:03:39,614 --> 01:03:40,735
