Riley McCormick from Canada.

1139
01:47:41,063 --> 01:47:42,627
13th.

1140
01:47:44,811 --> 01:47:53,694
Diving to give Canada a representative in the concluding event in the pool tonight.

1141
01:47:54,114 --> 01:47:55,478
Back three and a half somersault.

1142
01:48:01,837 --> 01:48:03,498
pressure on this dive.

1143
01:48:04,680 --> 01:48:06,082
One outside the top twelve.

1144
01:48:07,724 --> 01:48:09,166
Oh, spectacularly good.

1145
01:48:12,289 --> 01:48:13,390
High tariff with this one.

1146
01:48:13,411 --> 01:48:15,673
It was his best dive last night.

1147
01:48:15,833 --> 01:48:16,956
He obviously likes this one.

1148
01:48:16,996 --> 01:48:18,356
He saves his best till last.

1149
01:48:22,381 --> 01:48:27,609
Canada have picked up two bronze in these Olympic Games in the diving and they they'll want to be here competing tonight.

1150
01:48:28,048 --> 01:48:29,872
Not just as spectators.

1151
01:48:30,112 --> 01:48:31,033
Boy, he might have done it.

1152
01:48:34,237 --> 01:48:39,640
A big sprinkling of nines across the scoreboard for him.

1153
01:48:41,542 --> 01:48:47,069
And Matthew Mitchum can only applaud the work of his opponent here, 97.2.

1154
01:48:47,090 --> 01:48:51,235
Whoa, that's one of the top dives of the night.

1155
01:48:52,818 --> 01:48:54,880
Talk about digging deep when it's necessary.

1156
01:48:56,542 --> 01:49:03,211
Heinkler Aguila is bringing up the bottom of the table at the moment.

1157
01:49:03,230 --> 01:49:08,698
Back two and a half, somersault two and a half twist to end his Olympic campaign.

1158
01:49:14,533 --> 01:49:15,574
better finish from him.

1159
01:49:16,015 --> 01:49:20,381
Pretty disappointing considering he came in as the tenth qualifier.

1160
01:49:28,113 --> 01:49:34,442
Couldn't make the final in Beijing and again, it's a semifinal ranking for him.

1161
01:49:34,462 --> 01:49:41,131
Top eighteen in the world.

1162
01:49:43,069 --> 01:49:54,583
Now there's a lot of pressure on this dive for Matthew Mitchum who's coming in to his last dive ranked 11th but those around him are really finding extra points with their last dive.

1163
01:49:55,185 --> 01:50:04,515
The Olympic champion wants the chance to defend that title tonight and cannot afford anything less than his best now.

1164
01:50:05,117 --> 01:50:06,417
It's his highest tariff dive.

1165
01:50:08,900 --> 01:50:10,984
Back two and a half somersault, two and a half twist.

1166
01:50:15,131 --> 01:50:16,554
Oh, I don't know.

1167
01:50:16,573 --> 01:50:17,836
I don't know.

1168
01:50:17,855 --> 01:50:24,127
Some concerned faces amongst those interested in his outcome.

1169
01:50:24,967 --> 01:50:26,109
This was a big splash.

1170
01:50:30,016 --> 01:50:34,143
Looked to be struggling and I think we've just lost him.

1171
01:50:35,164 --> 01:50:36,346
These scores aren't enough.

1172
01:50:37,390 --> 01:50:39,592
And that will be a loss to tonight's final.

1173
01:50:39,653 --> 01:50:44,599
He was still one of the big names being mentioned in the medal frame coming into this competition.

1174
01:50:44,639 --> 01:50:50,725
And it will be a real shock and a real story if Matthew Mitchum has missed that cut.

1175
01:50:51,667 --> 01:50:55,551
And he is flirting with it on those marks, Steve.

1176
01:50:56,052 --> 01:51:00,878
Well, that 70.2 is his lowest scoring dive of the night and had the highest tariff.

1177
01:51:00,899 --> 01:51:03,481
So I should say morning again.

1178
01:51:04,912 --> 01:51:26,516
a man who produced the the end dive to end all end dives four years ago is suffering the opposite now nick mccrory's got his own worries he's 10th back two and a half somersault two and a half twist needs a steady points return i think that was steady enough

1179
01:51:30,479 --> 01:51:31,780
Good push off the platform.

1180
01:51:33,523 --> 01:51:35,626
One of the taller divers here, 5'11".

1181
01:51:35,725 --> 01:51:41,233
It's a lot of body to get around and up into the air, but he does it very efficiently.

1182
01:51:41,273 --> 01:51:47,220
And he should be OK.

1183
01:51:51,145 --> 01:51:51,886
In fact, he will be.

1184
01:51:52,327 --> 01:51:54,510
Look at the number of competitors left and where he sits.

1185
01:51:55,992 --> 01:51:56,773
McCrory's in.

1186
01:51:57,900 --> 01:52:02,305
Alexander Bondar, ninth after five dives.

1187
01:52:02,426 --> 01:52:08,051
Back two and a half somersault, two and a half twist, looking over his shoulder.

1188
01:52:17,622 --> 01:52:18,462
Very nice entry.

1189
01:52:21,287 --> 01:52:21,787
Bondor.

1190
01:52:23,469 --> 01:52:25,631
Oh, there is the disappointment of Matthew Mitchum.

1191
01:52:25,650 --> 01:52:27,233
I think he knows he's gone.

1192
01:52:29,422 --> 01:52:30,744
tearful end to his campaign.

1193
01:52:30,784 --> 01:52:36,332
The leg form here, Londa not so special and 79.2.

1194
01:52:36,551 --> 01:52:50,149
One of his lower rank dives for the session but he's okay, he's qualified.

1195
01:52:51,900 --> 01:52:57,212
on our little scoreboard here up in our commentary position as it's confirmed who can't be displaced.

1196
01:52:57,292 --> 01:53:03,725
A little Q is coming up next to their name but Mitcham knows it's no final for him.

1197
01:53:04,506 --> 01:53:08,033
Even Garcia eighth.

1198
01:53:08,052 --> 01:53:13,824
Finishing with a forward two and a half somersault with three twists with a 3.8 tariff.

1199
01:53:15,306 --> 01:53:16,988
didn't finish it as he would have liked.

1200
01:53:17,710 --> 01:53:26,840
Head came down pretty quickly as he looked to get into the twisting section of his dive and over the legs come.

1201
01:53:36,992 --> 01:53:37,972
That should do it though.

1202
01:53:44,635 --> 01:53:45,475
And a 79.8.

1203
01:53:45,735 --> 01:53:46,356
So he's in.

1204
01:53:46,617 --> 01:53:57,649
It's been a strange session, though, for this man.

1205
01:53:57,970 --> 01:54:03,336
German Sanchez, who was looking very impressive at one stage, but he's fallen away.

1206
01:54:03,917 --> 01:54:07,520
He's back down in 14th, forward four and a half somersault, 3.7.

1207
01:54:07,640 --> 01:54:11,385
Needs a big haul from that.

1208
01:54:15,431 --> 01:54:24,384
Twenty-year-old from Guadalajara, silver medallist in the synchro with Ivan Garcia, does not want to be split from his countrymen for tonight.

1209
01:54:25,706 --> 01:54:29,730
This was his lowest scoring dive in the prelims.

1210
01:54:30,351 --> 01:54:31,613
I think he's making amends here.

1211
01:54:31,634 --> 01:54:42,368
He only got sixes for it last night, but today some eights and a good tariff of three-seven.

1212
01:54:44,018 --> 01:54:45,279
And an eighty-eight point eight.

1213
01:54:54,789 --> 01:54:55,310
He's waiting.

1214
01:54:56,692 --> 01:55:00,735
Martin Wolfram in fifth place.

1215
01:55:00,957 --> 01:55:02,719
Forward four and a half somersault to end.

1216
01:55:02,738 --> 01:55:06,802
Three point seven the tariff.

1217
01:55:09,431 --> 01:55:10,073
Very nice.

1218
01:55:10,212 --> 01:55:12,376
A little short on the entry.

1219
01:55:13,077 --> 01:55:13,597
Not much.

1220
01:55:14,399 --> 01:55:15,279
And a big tariff.

1221
01:55:21,809 --> 01:55:23,811
He's had a good competition so far though.

1222
01:55:25,673 --> 01:55:34,966
Responding to the challenge of this, the very highest level of competition which is pretty new to him.

1223
01:55:37,411 --> 01:55:47,844
They're all in.

1224
01:55:48,385 --> 01:55:57,015
Sasha Klein in sixth place will also looking to be joining the party and should do unless something disastrous happens to his back.

1225
01:55:57,034 --> 01:55:59,097
Two and a half somersault, two and a half twists.

1226
01:56:02,301 --> 01:56:03,363
He's been consistent.

1227
01:56:04,384 --> 01:56:10,050
Well, no disaster there, but not quite what he would like to show us in the final, but he'll be there.

1228
01:56:10,090 --> 01:56:28,247
The judge is very much of the same view about this dive, which got him 81 in the prelims.

1229
01:56:30,350 --> 01:56:30,789
And again.

1230
01:56:33,216 --> 01:56:37,481
Nothing if not consistent.

1231
01:56:37,502 --> 01:56:38,944
Now, the battle within the battle.

1232
01:56:39,645 --> 01:56:52,819
Lin Yue from China, second behind his countrymen, back two and a half somersault, two and a half twists to conclude an impressive program.

1233
01:56:57,326 --> 01:56:58,466
Well, impressive again.

1234
01:56:59,247 --> 01:57:02,532
Lin Yue, there was a little bit of a leg form break at the top of the dive.

1235
01:57:03,018 --> 01:57:05,140
But he got it all back together very neatly.

1236
01:57:07,703 --> 01:57:14,431
Just there the ankles drifted apart but restores his usual immaculate position as he enters the water.

1237
01:57:23,341 --> 01:57:27,606
So, will it be China 1-2 going into the final?

1238
01:57:28,889 --> 01:57:30,831
These scores don't carry forward of course, Roger.

1239
01:57:32,988 --> 01:57:43,960
They may well carry forward in one or two divers' minds as they see the standards that the Chinese divers have set, not that it comes as any surprise at all.

1240
01:57:46,023 --> 01:57:51,828
And leading the field has been 19-year-old Chu Bo, the bookie's favourite.

1241
01:57:54,112 --> 01:57:56,194
Back two and a half somersault, two and a half twist.

1242
01:57:59,077 --> 01:58:02,079
Well, why not end the session with something near perfection?

1243
01:58:02,940 --> 01:58:06,725
Troubo could give us another 100-point dive here.

1244
01:58:06,784 --> 01:58:10,770
Such power off the platform.

1245
01:58:12,431 --> 01:58:13,573
